  "model": "gpt-5.6-terra",
  "reasoning_effort": "high",
  "prompt": "prompts/physics_committee_terra_round2_v1.md",
  "preferred_configuration": {
    "prize_parts": [
      {
        "ballot_id": "B021",
        "laureates": [
          "Harald Rose",
          "Max Haider",
          "Knut Urban"
        ],
        "citation": "for spherical-aberration correction in transmission electron microscopy"
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B048",
    "B037"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "My configuration has not changed. B021 remains a sharply bounded invention that made atomic-scale structural and chemical observation a reproducible experimental capability, rather than a cosmetic increment in imaging. Its maturity is evident in the durable, independently validated role of corrected TEM across materials physics. Rose, Haider, and Urban remain the proposed chain of credit from correction concepts to practical realization and demonstration, subject to the priority review specified by the chair.",
    "case_against": "The remaining reservation is substantial and concerns exact credit, not the importance of the instrument. Electron-optical correction involved theoretical precursors, instrument engineering, and later development, so the historical record must establish the distinct original roles of Rose, Haider, and Urban and prevent the citation from absorbing broader corrected-electron-microscopy advances.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "kroll-stefan",
        "point": "Kroll prefers B048 because optical lattice clocks are mature, reproducible, and comparatively cleanly attributable to Katori and Ye, while noting that B021 needs close historical reconstruction across theory, engineering, and implementation.",
        "response": "I agree that B048 is an exceptionally strong alternative and that its focused two-person allocation is an important advantage. I nevertheless retain B021 because spherical-aberration correction opened a directly observable regime in matter and has a narrowly identifiable original instrumental achievement. The unresolved B021 credit question should be settled by priority evidence, not inferred from the breadth of its later adoption."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "eriksson-olle",
        "point": "Eriksson regards B043 as a mature theory-to-experiment discovery of the quantum spin Hall effect and regards B021 as a leading alternative whose credit chain needs careful delimitation.",
        "response": "His distinction between a clear physical discovery and a technique is useful, but in this case the instrument is itself the invention that changed the accessible physical evidence. Corrected TEM permits matter to be measured atom by atom with durable experimental consequences. B043 remains scientifically compelling, yet its boundary from previously recognized topological physics is less settled than the physical scope of B021."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "johansson-goran",
        "point": "Johansson emphasizes that B048 rests on the magic-wavelength lattice-clock architecture rather than record precision alone and requires a citation bounded from wider optical-frequency metrology.",
        "response": "I agree with this emphasis and retain B048 as the principal alternative. It also reinforces the appropriate standard for B021: our citation should identify spherical-aberration correction itself, not claim all later electron-microscopy performance or applications. Both cases require disciplined historical boundaries; B021 still offers the more immediate expansion of what can be experimentally seen."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "Whether archival priority evidence confirms the precise respective original contributions of Rose, Haider, Urban, and other electron-optics contributors to the first successful corrected TEM instrument and demonstration.",
      "Whether the citation can be confined rigorously to spherical-aberration correction rather than broader corrected-electron-microscopy development.",
      "Whether B048's attribution can ultimately be limited to Katori and Ye after comparable historical review."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile; no profile-based connection to the proposed laureates or achievement has been identified."
  }
}
